 hook='Zzz... SNORE! 😴 What if you snored every single night? Is it just noisy, or could it be a warning sign? KOMO listens closely.',
 how='When you sleep, the muscles in your throat relax. The airway gets narrower, and air squeezing through makes soft tissues like the soft palate and uvula vibrate. That vibration is the snoring sound. Sleeping on your back, a blocked nose, alcohol, extra weight and tiredness can all make snoring louder.',
